chessKRK: a UCI engine for pawnless chess endings, built as the case study of
the paper on the "hide what varies" meta-principle, with its ArchUnit rules,
the naive version (Before/) and its refactoring (After/), Martin's examples as
code (Examples/), the external oracles (Oracles/), the scripts and the docs.
